# ===========================================================================
# ALLOWLIST, not a blocklist.
#
# Everything is ignored, and the few paths that belong in a public repository
# are added back one at a time.  Same reasoning as app/tools/release_audit.py:
# the failure modes are not symmetric.  Forgetting to exclude something
# publishes it -- silently, permanently, and to everyone.  Forgetting to
# include something produces an obvious "it doesn't run" that gets fixed in a
# minute.  A blocklist fails in the direction that matters.
#
# WHAT THIS IS KEEPING OUT OF A PUBLIC REPO
# -----------------------------------------
#   extracted/, app.asar  -- the unpacked Legends of Idleon client.  That is
#                            Lava Flame Studios' copyrighted game, not ours to
#                            redistribute; publishing it invites a takedown.
#   bot/recordings/       -- 3+ GB of full-screen capture of a live account:
#                            character names, progress, passers-by.
#   _dev/, sushi_unknown/ -- screenshots taken mid-session, same problem.
#   dist/                 -- build output, including an 89 MB exe.
#
# Before your first push, run:  git status --short
# Anything listed that is not app/, web/ or a root .md file is a bug in here.
# ===========================================================================

# Ignore everything at the root...
/*

# ...then allow only these back.
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/README.md
!/LICENSE
!/RELEASING.md
!/app/
!/web/

# --- working data inside app/, which the allowlist would otherwise let in ---
# These mirror DENY in app/tools/release_audit.py.  Keep the two in step: that
# file governs what enters the exe, this one governs what enters the repo, and
# a folder that is unsafe to ship is unsafe to publish.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
sushi_unknown/
wind_unknown/
sushi_label/
misses/
recordings/
hoops_stats.json
*.png.bak

# Local run data, if it ever lands in the tree rather than %APPDATA%.
*.log
debug/
